; [CHOSEN, not recovered] - DICE's own .def is not in the shipped image, but its EFFECT is.
; `dumpbin /exports AIDLL_w32ded.dll` on the reference binary
; ("D:\B2BF Launcher\Battlefield2\AIDLL_w32ded.dll", image base 0x10000000) returns exactly two
; names, undecorated, in this order:
;
;     ordinal hint RVA      name
;           1    0 000637E0 deinitDll
;           2    1 00063340 initDll
;
; plus the CRT entry point DllEntryPoint at 0x101E2C31, which is not an EXPORTS entry.
;
; The ordinals are pinned to match the shipped image. The engine resolves both by NAME
; (`GetProcAddress(h, "initDll")` in dice::hfe::LoadLibraryBf, Core/PluginDll.cpp), so the ordinals
; are cosmetic; matching them keeps a dumpbin diff of the two images clean. Same reasoning, and the
; same two names, as Code/SwiffPlayerAbi/SwiffPlayer.def.
;
; ⚠ NO `LIBRARY` STATEMENT. The link already names the image AIDLL_w32ded.dll; a LIBRARY line here
; would only duplicate it, and link.exe warns when the two disagree.
;
; NOTHING ELSE MAY BE ADDED HERE. The two-export surface IS the side-DLL ABI - see
; Code/BF2/Core/DllModule.h ("the whole contract between the server and a module is: hand over the
; ClassManager, get a bool back, and later say stop"). Everything the host needs beyond these
; crosses through IClassManager and the simple-singleton registry, never through a symbol.
;
; ⚠ BOTH ARE `extern "C"` INSIDE `dice::hfe`, which is what makes the exported names undecorated
; while the ELF assert still prints `bool dice::hfe::initDll(dice::hfe::IClassManager*)`.
; Core/DllModule.h records that pair; the declarations there are what this file exports.
EXPORTS
    deinitDll   @1
    initDll     @2
